        "timestamp": 1775206421,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Hegseth ousts US Army chief of staff Issued on: 03/04/2026 - 10:53 Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth has asked General Randy George to step down as chief of staff of the US Army, an official said Thursday. The official, who spoke on condition of anonymity, confirmed a report from US broadcaster CBS that said George had been asked to take immediate retirement. The reason for the request was not immediately known, but CBS quoted a source as saying Hegseth wanted someone who would implement his and President Donald Trump's vision for the Army. UN Security Council to vote on authorizing force to protect Hormuz 03/04/2026 ‘Disturbing trend’ of US-Israeli strikes hitting non-military targets in Iran 03/04/2026 Middle East Trump sacks attorney general, replaces with ex-personal lawyer 02/04/2026 Americas 'Any weapon Europe buys from the US is a liability', rearmament expert says 02/04/2026 Europe Trump sacks attorney general Bondi, Hegseth asks US Army Chief of Staff to step down 02/04/2026 Americas Macron says Trump marriage jibe does not 'merit response' 02/04/2026 France 'He wasn't convincing to the world and to the American people', former US ambassador to NATO says 02/04/2026 Americas Europe, NATO under pressure over Iran war: 'Trump strong with the weak and weak with the strong' 02/04/2026 Middle East Thomas Pesquet on space exploration: 'We’re all on the same boat, we have to take care of the ship' 02/04/2026 Science"
