        "timestamp": 1775206366,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. UN Security Council to vote on authorizing force to protect Hormuz Issued on: 03/04/2026 - 10:52 The UN Security Council will vote Friday on a draft resolution brought by Bahrain to authorize the use of \"defensive\" force to protect shipping in the Strait of Hormuz from Iranian attacks. Iran has placed a stranglehold on the key shipping lane -- threatening fuel supplies and roiling the global economy -- in retaliation for US-Israeli strikes that triggered the month-old Middle East war. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Andrew Hilliar tells us more. Hegseth ousts US Army chief of staff 03/04/2026 ‘Disturbing trend’ of US-Israeli strikes hitting non-military targets in Iran 03/04/2026 Middle East Trump sacks attorney general, replaces with ex-personal lawyer 02/04/2026 Americas 'Any weapon Europe buys from the US is a liability', rearmament expert says 02/04/2026 Europe Trump sacks attorney general Bondi, Hegseth asks US Army Chief of Staff to step down 02/04/2026 Americas Macron says Trump marriage jibe does not 'merit response' 02/04/2026 France 'He wasn't convincing to the world and to the American people', former US ambassador to NATO says 02/04/2026 Americas Europe, NATO under pressure over Iran war: 'Trump strong with the weak and weak with the strong' 02/04/2026 Middle East Thomas Pesquet on space exploration: 'We’re all on the same boat, we have to take care of the ship' 02/04/2026 Science"
